WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.240
...are quite wide. It's sometimes difficult

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:04.400
to get pieces that are big enough.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.040
Usually, little teeny pieces sit too low.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.360
So, in order to fill a space,

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.320
this is a way that I often deal with it.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.639
I'll get framed pictures such as this

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:17.279
that are tall so that they fill the area.

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:20.200
So, I have three of these, and I'm going
to stack these down the center.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.800
Now, for most people, when they're
putting together shelves,

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.280
they automatically think of shelves
as being side to side.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:46.559
They don't think about center.

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:50.320
I like to start in the middle and work out
because, to me, that's the

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.480
best way to eliminate clutter.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.640
Most people feel comfortable when they have

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.039
a horizon line and they have symmetry.

00:00:57.039 --> 00:01:00.239
And that's what we're trying to create
when we're looking at these shelves.

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:03.120
Adding those pictures to the center
do exactly that.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.840
So, I start building my vignette
out from the—
